{"id":"R0001","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","primary":"","reason":"Awaiting classification because R0001 is a 3-page ICWS 2026 Work-in-Progress paper (CWS_WIP_222) and Fig. 2 and Fig. 3 are missing from page 3 of the PDF, leaving reported evaluation results and metrics unverified.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","this paper proposes a Cloud-Edge-End Adaptive Partitioning and Resource Allocation method","Proposes CAPRI optimization and PPO-based orchestration for collaborative inference.","PDF"],"E2":["T",3,"III. EXPERIMENT EVALUATION / A. Simulation Setup","This experiment considers 10 UAVs, 4 ESs and one cloud server.","Evaluated setting explicitly includes 10 UAVs, 4 ESs, and 1 cloud server.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"II. SYSTEM MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION / A. Inference Partitioning","Previous inference service is calculated on UAV, the middle part is completes on ES","Partitions DNN layers at pk and qk across UAVs, ESs, and cloud.","PDF"],"E4":["U",3,"III. EXPERIMENT EVALUATION / A. Simulation Setup","Fig. 2 illustrates the reward convergence of all algorithms","Simulation setup is described, but Fig. 2 and Fig. 3 plots/metrics are missing from the PDF.","PDF"],"E5":["T",0,"ICWS 2026 – Program","13-18 July 2026, Sydney, Australia","Conference held 13-18 July 2026 (PDF downloaded 24 Nov 2026), before 2026-11-26.","https://services.conferences.computer.org/2026/icws-program/"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) provides flexible and mobile deployment capabilities","Full 3-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["U",0,"ICWS 2026 – Program (CWS-WIP-S3)","CWS_WIP_222: Adaptive Partition and Resource Allocation for Collaborative Inference Services in UAV Swarm","Peer-reviewed per ICWS 2026 CFP, but WIP track (CWS_WIP_222) and missing PDF figures prevent verifying evaluation results.","https://services.conferences.computer.org/2026/icws-program/"]}}
{"id":"R0002","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this peer-reviewed ICWS 2026 regular paper evaluating collaborative ResNet-18 inference migration across 30 UAVs in three swarms.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose a predictive and cost-optimal migration scheme, named Promise","Proposes Promise with LST-GNN prediction and PDBH migration optimization.","PDF"],"E2":["T",7,"VII. EXPERIMENTS AND ANALYSIS / A. Experimental Settings","the numbers of UAVs in the three swarms are set to 5, 10, and 15","Evaluated with 30 UAVs across three swarms (5, 10, and 15 UAVs).","PDF"],"E3":["T",7,"VII. EXPERIMENTS AND ANALYSIS / A. Experimental Settings","Each generated task is equally partition into two task modules","Partitions ResNet-18 inference into two modules distributed and migrated across UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",7,"VII. EXPERIMENTS AND ANALYSIS / B. Evaluation of Promise","success rates of task execution are shown in Fig. 3.","Evaluates ResNet-18/CIFAR-10 against 4 baselines on success rate, migration cost, and accuracy.","PDF"],"E5":["T",0,"ICWS 2026 – Program","13-18 July 2026, Sydney, Australia","Conference held 13-18 July 2026 (PDF downloaded 25 Nov 2026), before 2026-11-26.","https://services.conferences.computer.org/2026/icws-program/"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","In multi-UAV networks, reliable and continuous UAV services providing edge intelligence","Full 9-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",0,"Info for Authors – Peer Review Policy","All submitted manuscripts will be peer-reviewed by at least three members of the program committee.","Peer-reviewed ICWS 2026 regular paper (CWS_REG_116) with LST-GNN/PDBH method and Figs. 3-5 results.","https://services.conferences.computer.org/2026/info-for-authors/"]}}
{"id":"R0003","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2023 IEEE WCSP conference paper evaluating dynamic switching to multi-UAV collaborative VGG16 inference across 4 to 8 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose an algorithm called Dynamic Model Switching (DMS) based on genetic algorithms","Proposes DMS genetic algorithm for UAV swarm collaborative inference.","PDF"],"E2":["T",6,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS / B. Results Analysis","we further investigated the utility values under different numbers of UAVs","Evaluates swarms of 4 to 8 UAVs (and 5 UAVs in Table 1).","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"III. SYSTEM MODEL / B. Latency Model For Executing Large Complex Model","large complex model needs to be partitioned and executed on different UAVs.","Switches between single-UAV small CNN and multi-UAV layer-partitioned VGG16 inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",5,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS / A. Simulation Settings","trajectories of the UAVs in our simulation are based on the real-world trajectory traces","Trace-driven simulation comparing DMS to 4 baselines on utility, latency, and accuracy.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2023 IEEE the 15th International Conference on Wireless Communications and Signal Processing","Published in 2023, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs), or say drones have gained widespread popularity","Full 7-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2023 International Conference on Wireless Communications and Signal Processing (WCSP)","IEEE WCSP 2023 conference proceedings paper with GA-based DMS method and Table 1/Figs. 2-3 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0006","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2025 IEEE ICPADS conference paper evaluating joint UAV deployment and DNN layer partitioning across 5 to 10 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we proposes AirInfer, an innovative collaborative UAV inference framework with critical zones coverage.","Proposes AirInfer framework jointly optimizing DNN partitioning and UAV deployment.","PDF"],"E2":["T",6,"V. EXPERIMENTAL EVALUATION / B. Effectiveness of the Proposed Algorithm","we first detail the optimization process for a configuration of five UAVs","Evaluated with 5 UAVs (and 5 to 10 UAVs in Fig. 6a).","PDF"],"E3":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","how to partition a deep learning model across a UAV swarm for collaborative inference","Partitions chain-structured DNN layers across UAVs with inter-UAV activation transfer.","PDF"],"E4":["T",6,"V. EXPERIMENTAL EVALUATION / A. Experimental Setup","All results, averaged over 100 trials with a coverage threshold","100-trial simulation comparing AirInfer to 3 baselines on latency and coverage.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2025 IEEE 31th International Conference on Parallel and Distributed Systems (ICPADS)","Published in 2025, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Driven by falling prices and advancing technology, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs)","Full 8-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2025 IEEE 31th International Conference on Parallel and Distributed Systems (ICPADS)","IEEE ICPADS 2025 conference proceedings paper with DP+SCA method and Figs. 3-6 latency/coverage results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0009","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this peer-reviewed IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems article evaluating collaborative DNN partitioning across 4 UAVs and ground users.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose a Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL)-based DNN Partitioning and Dynamic Trajectory Selection (DPDTS) method","Proposes DPDTS combining OPPS, fairness matching, and TD3 trajectory optimization.","PDF"],"E2":["T",8,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS / A. Simulation Settings","The flying height H of four UAVs is 50m.","Evaluated in a multi-UAV MEC system with 4 UAVs and 50-90 GUs.","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"III. SYSTEM MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION","The first half of each task of the ith GU is executed locally","Partitions DNN inference (ResNet-34, VGG-16, AlexNet) between GUs and UAV edge servers.","PDF"],"E4":["T",8,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS / B. Performance Evaluation","we analyze the total energy consumption of the system as well as the average task processing latency","Simulations over 50 episodes comparing DPDTS to 4 baselines on energy and latency.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Footnote","Date of publication 13 November 2025; date of current version 26 December 2025.","Published online 13 Nov 2025 (Jan 2026 issue), before 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Intelligent air-ground integration communication is an emerging technology.","Full 11-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Footnote","Received 13 January 2025; revised 3 July 2025 and 23 September 2025; accepted 19 October 2025.","Peer-reviewed IEEE TITS journal article with OPPS/DPDTS method and Figs. 4-8 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0010","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2024 IEEE WCNC conference paper evaluating pipelined collaborative DNN inference across 5 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose an efficient solution exploiting deep reinforcement learning (DRL) with action space simplification","Proposes DRL-based pipeline collaborative DNN inference allocation with action disassembly.","PDF"],"E2":["T",5,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS AND EVALUATION / B. Results Analysis","involving the use of 5 UAVs to perform 10 VGG-16 inference tasks.","Evaluated with 5 UAVs executing pipelined AlexNet, GoogLeNet, and VGG-16 tasks.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"III. MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION / A. System Model","The DNN model is divided into multiple parts in the UAV swarm","Partitions DNN layers sequentially across N UAVs in a pipeline.","PDF"],"E4":["T",5,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS AND EVALUATION / A. Simulation Settings","we use existing UAV trajectory data [22] and calculate the transmission rate","Trace-driven simulation comparing to 5 baselines on reward and completion latency.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2024 IEEE Wireless Communications and Networking Conference (WCNC)","Published in 2024, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Recent advancements in unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) technology have propelled","Full 6-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2024 IEEE Wireless Communications and Networking Conference (WCNC)","IEEE WCNC 2024 conference proceedings paper with DRL pipeline method and Figs. 3-5 latency results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0015","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2023 IEEE BigCom conference paper evaluating fine-grained collaborative CNN inference across 3 to 11 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we introduce an online heuristic solution, namely EECIA, to find the computing task allocation strategy","Proposes EECIA online heuristic for fine-grained collaborative DNN inference in UAV swarms.","PDF"],"E2":["T",6,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND EVALUATION / B. Results Analysis","use three UAVs to collaboratively execute inference task of AlexNet, five UAVs to execute ResNet152 and VGG-16.","Evaluated with 3 to 11 UAVs across AlexNet, ResNet152, and VGG-16.","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"III. MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION / A. System Model","calculation of one layer can be divided into multiple subtasks and allocated to multiple UAVs","Distributes CNN layers and intra-layer subtasks across UAVs for collaborative inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",6,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND EVALUATION / B. Results Analysis","we show the performance comparison of our method and four benchmark schemes","Simulations comparing EECIA to 4 baselines on inference latency and algorithm runtime.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2023 9th International Conference on Big Data Computing and Communications (BIGCOM)","Published in 2023, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","In recent years, with the development of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) technology","Full 8-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2023 9th International Conference on Big Data Computing and Communications (BigCom)","IEEE BigCom 2023 conference proceedings paper with EECIA method and Table II/Figs. 3-5 latency results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0019","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this peer-reviewed IEEE Internet of Things Journal article evaluating PPO-based trajectory planning and distributed CNN inference across 2 to 5 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","this article introduces a real-time and dynamic solution for online applications using deep reinforcement learning.","Proposes PPO-based joint trajectory planning and distributed CNN inference.","PDF"],"E2":["T",15,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND ANALYSIS","Fig. 18 refers to the comparison between swarms enclosing different numbers of UAVs","Evaluated with 2 to 5 UAVs (3, 4, 5 UAVs in Figs. 8, 18, 19).","PDF"],"E3":["T",4,"III. DISTRIBUTED CNN AND PATH PLANNING / A. System Model","Each layer will be assigned to one UAV, and based on the UAV capabilities","Distributes CNN layers (LeNet, AlexNet, VGG16) across connected UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",11,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND ANALYSIS","we evaluate our system in terms of the accuracy of respecting different constraints, the latency","Simulations comparing PPO to ILP, Actor-Critic, OULD, heuristic, and random baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Footnote","Date of publication 28 December 2022; date of current version 25 April 2023.","Published online Dec 2022 / issue May 2023, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Some UAV applications require more than one device to accomplish their mission","Full 17-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Footnote","Manuscript received 8 July 2022; revised 15 October 2022; accepted 9 December 2022.","Peer-reviewed IEEE IoT-J journal article with PPO method and Figs. 4-19 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0022","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2025 IEEE ICCT conference paper evaluating Option-Critic HRL collaborative early-exit inference across 8 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose a collaborative strategy based on hierarchical reinforcement learning (HRL)","Proposes Option-Critic HRL integrating early-exit selection and model partitioning.","PDF"],"E2":["T",5,"IV. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION / TABLE I","N | 8","Evaluated with N=8 UAVs (plus group owner) in a serverless multi-UAV swarm.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"II. SYSTEM MODEL","the model is partitioned into segments that can be processed across multiple UAVs.","Partitions AlexNet layers up to selected early-exit point across multiple UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",5,"IV. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","We have defined three baseline methods for comparison","Simulations on AlexNet comparing to PSO-GA, DQN, and Min-Cost Exit on reward, energy, and time.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2025 IEEE 25th International Conference on Communication Technology (ICCT)","Published in 2025, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","The rapid growth of the Internet of Things (IoT) and artificial intelligence (AI)","Full 6-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2025 IEEE 25th International Conference on Communication Technology","IEEE ICCT 2025 conference proceedings paper with Option-Critic method and Figs. 3-6 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0029","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2022 IEEE IWCMC conference paper evaluating DQN-based reliable DNN partitioning and replication across 11 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose a deep Q learning-based DNN partitioning strategy for minimizing the energy consumption","Proposes DQN-based reliable DNN partitioning with active replication across UAVs.","PDF"],"E2":["T",5,"IV. EXPERIMENTS RESULTS AND ANALYSIS / A. Simulation Setup","We assume that the UAVs including the group owner are 11, i.e., N = 10","Evaluated with 11 UAVs (group owner plus 10 nearby UAVs).","PDF"],"E3":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","dividing the DNN into several subtasks and offloading among UAVs","Partitions DAG-structured DNN layers with active replicas across multiple UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",5,"IV. EXPERIMENTS RESULTS AND ANALYSIS / B. Experiments Analysis","we compare the proposed DQN-based algorithm with other three benchmarks.","Simulations on AlexNet, VGG19, GoogleNet, ResNet101 comparing energy under deadlines and failures.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2022 International Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing (IWCMC)","Published in 2022, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","The UAV swarm, which consists of several UAVs [1], has demonstrated great potential","Full 6-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2022 International Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing (IWCMC)","IEEE IWCMC 2022 conference proceedings paper with DQN partitioning method and Figs. 4-5 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0044","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All eligibility criteria E1-E7 are established for this 2024 IEEE ISPCE-ASIA conference paper evaluating collaborative DNN partitioning and offloading across 4 UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose the master problem as a non-convex optimization problem and the LaCPOO algorithm","Proposes CVaR-based robust transmission and Bat-inspired CPOO/LaCPOO DNN partitioning.","PDF"],"E2":["T",6,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS / A. Simulation Setup and Pameters","with UAV clusters including 4 UAVs as edge servers.","Evaluated with a cluster of 4 UAVs serving mobile devices in a 400m x 400m area.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"II. SYSTEM MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION / A. System Overview","The subtasks can be offloaded to the UAVs for cooperative computing.","Partitions DNN layers along output rows (AIR) and offloads subtasks across multiple UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",7,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS / B. Experiments Analysis","our proposed LaCPOO algorithm can provide the lowest average delay even in uncertain environments","Simulations on AlexNet, NiN, TinyYOLOv2, VGG16 comparing delay and power against 3 baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Header","2024 IEEE International Symposium on Product Compliance Engineering - Asia (ISPCE-ASIA)","Published in 2024, wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","With the explosion of the Internet of Things (IoT) and artificial intelligence (AI)","Full 8-page text is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","2024 IEEE International Symposium on Product Compliance Engineering - Asia (ISPCE-ASIA)","IEEE ISPCE-ASIA 2024 proceedings paper with CVaR/LaCPOO method and Figs. 3-8 results.","PDF"]}}
